  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the skeptical expression of Arnold Schwarzenegger",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of Arnold Schwarzenegger, who is depicted with a skeptical expression. This projection occurs because the meme's text 'who is it and what do they do' implicitly asks the viewer to consider themselves in the role of the confused or questioning observer, aligning with the visual cue of Schwarzenegger's expression. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the framing of the image and text creates an implicit identification with the skeptical persona, making the viewer feel as if they are the one questioning the identity or role of the subject — which is themselves in the context of the meme's usage.",
